---
title: Posting a tweet — from upload to follower timeline
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User (browser)
    participant W as web
    participant G as gateway
    participant T as tweet-service
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant S3 as S3
    participant Q as Event transport
    participant F as fanout-worker
    participant US as user-service
    participant R as Redis

    Note over U,S3: Media is uploaded directly — it never transits a pod

    U->>W: compose tweet with image
    W->>G: POST /api/v1/media/presign
    G->>T: presign request (JWT subject in header)
    T->>S3: generate presigned PUT URL
    T-->>G: { url, objectKey }
    G-->>W: { url, objectKey }
    W-->>U: presigned URL
    U->>S3: PUT image bytes (direct)

    Note over U,DB: The write path — tweet and event commit atomically

    U->>W: submit
    W->>G: POST /api/v1/tweets { body, objectKey, Idempotency-Key }
    G->>G: validate JWT, check rate limit, attach correlation ID
    G->>T: forward request

    rect rgb(235, 244, 255)
        Note over T,DB: single database transaction
        T->>DB: INSERT INTO tweets
        T->>DB: INSERT INTO outbox (tweet.created)
        DB-->>T: COMMIT
    end

    T-->>G: 201 Created
    G-->>W: 201 Created
    W-->>U: tweet appears optimistically

    Note over Q,R: Asynchronous fan-out — the user is no longer waiting

    T-)Q: publish tweet.created
    Q-)F: deliver event
    F->>US: GET /internal/users/{authorId}/followers
    US-->>F: follower IDs + author follower_count

    alt author has < 10,000 followers  (fan-out on write)
        loop for each follower
            F->>R: LPUSH timeline:{follower} tweetId
            F->>R: LTRIM timeline:{follower} 0 799
        end
    else author is a celebrity  (fan-out on read)
        F->>R: SADD celebrities {authorId}
        Note right of F: no per-follower writes —<br/>timeline-service merges<br/>these tweets at read time
    end

    Note over F,Q: On failure the message is retried 3 times,<br/>then moved to a DLQ and an alert fires
